---
import { profile } from "../data/profile";
const { education, skills } = profile;
---

<section
  id="about"
  aria-labelledby="about-heading"
  class="page-shell py-14 md:py-20"
>
  <div aria-hidden="true" class="h-0.5 w-8 rounded-full bg-accent"></div>
  <h2
    id="about-heading"
    class="mt-4 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-heading"
  >
    About
  </h2>

  {/*
    The "why these projects, not generic ones" answer the peer review
    (2026-09-11) said was the missing connective tissue. Kept specific on
    purpose: transit, one road with no crossing, the dry season in Mexico.
    A category label like "drawn to civic tech" is what used to be here, and
    it could have described anyone.
  */}
  <div class="mt-8 sm:flex sm:items-start sm:gap-8">
    {
      profile.headshot && (
        <img
          src={profile.headshot}
          alt=""
          width="256"
          height="256"
          class="mb-6 h-28 w-28 shrink-0 rounded-2xl border border-border object-cover sm:mb-0 sm:h-32 sm:w-32"
        />
      )
    }

    <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4 leading-relaxed text-body">
      <p>
        I'm a data science student at the University of Washington, working
        where machine learning meets data visualization, with a focus on
        turning analysis into decisions people can act on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Seattle is where I first relied on public transit. Getting to friends,
        to family, to the airport stopped being a problem I had to solve, and
        that is when city planning stopped being abstract to me. An apartment
        block and a supermarket separated by one road with no crossing is a
        decision somebody made, and the data behind decisions like it is
        usually public. That is what pulled me toward civic data.
      </p>
      <p>
        The environmental half is closer to home. I'm from Mexico, where the
        dry season is something you build against, and climate change keeps
        making it harder to plan for. Building energy filings sit exactly where
        those two interests meet, which is why the agent project runs on them
        and not on a sample dataset.
      </p>
      <p>
        At FCP Insight I build Python dashboards and data tooling that surface
        operational trends and inform planning decisions. I'm looking for
        new-grad roles where modeling and clear communication both matter.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div>
      <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-faint uppercase">
        Skills
      </h3>
      <dl class="mt-4 space-y-3">
        {
          skills.map((group) => (
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-0.5 text-sm sm:grid-cols-[7rem_1fr] sm:gap-3">
              <dt class="text-muted">{group.group}</dt>
              <dd class="text-body">{group.items.join(", ")}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div>
      <h3 class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-faint uppercase">
        Education
      </h3>
      <div class="mt-4 space-y-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
        <p class="font-medium text-heading">{education.school}</p>
        <p>{education.degree}</p>
        <p>Minor in {education.minor}</p>
        <p>{education.grad} · GPA {education.gpa}</p>
        {education.honors.map((honor) => <p>{honor}</p>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
